[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station with some of the regime influenced by a hydroelectric power scheme. GENERAL: Velocity area station. Stable gabion groyne control adequately gauged to bankfull. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). STATION HYDROMETRY: Cableway at a 35m wide river section located 400m downstream of the stage measuring site. Adequately gauged to bankfull. FLOW RECORD: Nov-Dec 2010 flows considered suspect due to extended period of freezing conditions. FLOW REGIME: Runoff (apart from compensation flows and spillage) from 14% of the upper catchment is diverted to the Shin hydroelectric power scheme. No significant surface storage.
CATCHMENT,Typical Highland mix of rough grazing and moorland with some afforestation.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to 2.960m with a measured flow of 219 cumecs. Floods spill out of bank around the station hut at around 2.7m.
Pooling Suitability,With a limited floodplain component, the extrapolation of the in-channel calibration will likely give a reasonable estimation of events above 3m, and hence this station is tentatively assigned pooling status.
[END]
